.\" dp(1) — manual page for dp, the project dev plan tracker.
.TH DP 1 "2026-10-04" "dp 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dp \- project dev plan, task and decision tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dp \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dp
tracks plans (milestones), tasks, and architecture decision records (ADRs)
for a single project in one SQLite database at
.IR .dp/dp.db .
Like
.BR git (1),
it locates the database by walking up from the current directory, so
commands work from any subdirectory. Run
.B "dp init"
in the project root once, before other commands.
.PP
The database uses WAL journaling, enforced foreign keys and a 5s busy
timeout; the schema is created on init and upgraded automatically when
a newer dp opens an older database. Commit
.I .dp/
to version control or add it to
.I .gitignore
as you prefer. Inspect the data directly with
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
If a database exists in the current directory or any parent, print its
path and change nothing. Otherwise create
.I .dp/dp.db
in the current directory and apply migrations. Idempotent.
.TP
.B task
Operate on tasks — the work items of a project.
.RS
.TP
.BI "add " TITLE
Create a new task.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIID\fR
Attach the task to plan \fIID\fR (must exist).
.TP
\fB\-\-due\fR \fIDATE\fR
Due date, \fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR
Priority; see
.BR PRIORITIES .
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tags\fR \fILIST\fR
Comma\-separated tags; surrounding whitespace is trimmed.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR
Long description, shown by \fBdp task show\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
Task type: \fIfeature\fR, \fIbug\fR, \fIchore\fR, \fIrefactor\fR or
\fIdocs\fR (default \fIfeature\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B list
Print tasks (table by default; see \fB\-\-format\fR). The default view is
pending tasks — \fItodo\fR, \fIactive\fR and \fIblocked\fR — ordered by
attention: \fIactive\fR first (work in progress), then \fIblocked\fR
(needs unblocking), then \fItodo\fR (queued), then by priority (urgent
first), due date (tasks without one last), and id.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIID\fR
Only tasks attached to plan \fIID\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-overdue\fR
Only tasks whose due date lies in the past; combines with the view flags
below.
.TP
\fB\-\-active\fR
Only tasks with status \fIactive\fR (currently being worked on).
.TP
\fB\-\-done\fR
Only completed tasks; takes precedence over \fB\-\-active\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
Only tasks of the given type: \fIfeature\fR, \fIbug\fR, \fIchore\fR,
\fIrefactor\fR or \fIdocs\fR.
.RE
.TP
.BI "show " ID
Print one task in full detail: status and its note, started/done
timestamps, resolution with note and duplicate linkage.
.TP
.BI "start " ID
Start working on a task: sets status to \fIactive\fR and records
\fIstarted_at\fR (first start only \(em restarting after an interruption
keeps the original timestamp). Idempotent for an already\-active task;
refuses from \fIdone\fR (reopen first). Active tasks sort to the top of
\fBdp task list\fR.
.TP
.BI "done " ID
Mark a task as done: sets status to \fIdone\fR, resolution to \fIdone\fR
and records \fIdone_at\fR. \fB\-\-note\fR \fITEXT\fR records scope
(e.g.\& \(dqbackend only\(dq). Idempotent \(em an already\-done task prints
a notice and is left unchanged. Reopen with
.BI "dp task mod " "ID \-\-status todo"
which clears \fIdone_at\fR and \fIresolution\fR.
.TP
.BI "abandon " ID
Mark a task as done with resolution \fIabandoned\fR and record
\fIdone_at\fR: the task was deliberately dropped unfinished.
\fB\-\-note\fR \fITEXT\fR records why \(em the top forgettable. Excluded
from the done counters in \fBdp stats\fR (output), but still listed by
\fBdp task list \-\-done\fR (history). Idempotent.
.TP
.BI "duplicate " ID
Close a task as a duplicate of another: resolution \fIduplicated\fR.
\fB\-\-of\fR \fIID\fR links the surviving task; \fB\-\-note\fR \fITEXT\fR
records why they were judged duplicates. Counts as output and plan
progress \(em the work was real, just misdirected.
.TP
.BI "rm " ID
Delete a task permanently. Always asks for confirmation (summary, then
y/N); \fB\-\-force\fR skips the prompt.
.TP
.BI "mod " ID
Change the given fields of a task; omitted flags leave the field
unchanged. With no flags at all, prints \(dqNothing to modify: no fields
given\(dq; with flags whose values equal the current ones, prints a notice
instead of writing. \fB\-\-note\fR requires \fB\-\-status\fR.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIID\fR
Reassign the task to plan \fIID\fR (must exist).
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fITEXT\fR
New title.
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fISTATUS\fR
New status; see
.BR STATES .
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fITEXT\fR
The reason for a status transition (blocked\-why, active\-context,
back\-to\-todo\-reason). Requires \fB\-\-status\fR; cleared on the next
transition — process\-scoped, unlike the permanent
\fIresolution_note\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR
New priority.
.TP
\fB\-\-due\fR \fIDATE\fR
New due date.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tags\fR \fILIST\fR
Replace the tag list.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR
New description.
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
New task type.
.RE
.RE
.TP
.B plan
Operate on plans (milestones / phases). A plan's
.I start_date
(when work is meant to begin) and
.I due_date
(deadline) form its schedule window; both are optional. Plans are
containers, not lifecycle entities: completion is derived from the
progress of their tasks; archiving is a deliberate act.
.RS
.TP
.BI "add " TITLE
Create a plan; accepts \fB\-\-adr\fR \fIID\fR (decision origin),
\fB\-\-due\fR \fIDATE\fR, \fB\-p\fR/\fB\-\-priority\fR and
\fB\-d\fR/\fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR.
.TP
.B list
Summarize plans with per\-plan progress (done/total, percentage).
.TP
.BI "show " ID
Print a plan in detail, its pending (not\-done) tasks, and how many
tasks in it are done.
.TP
.BI "archive " ID
Archive a plan — the container is closed for deliberate reasons; an
archived plan with partial progress is legitimate history.
.RE
.TP
.B adr
Operate on decision records (ADRs), displayed as \fIADR\-NNN\fR
(a render\-time format of the numeric id).
.RS
.TP
.BI "add " TITLE
Record a decision. \fB\-\-context\fR \fITEXT\fR and \fB\-\-decision\fR
\fITEXT\fR are required; \fB\-\-consequence\fR \fITEXT\fR is optional.
.TP
.BI "accept " ID
Accept a proposed (or rejected — verdicts can be revisited) decision.
Changing a previous verdict requires \fB\-\-rationale\fR \fITEXT\fR.
.TP
.BI "reject " ID
Reject a decision, optionally with \fB\-\-rationale\fR \fITEXT\fR.
Rejected decisions may be accepted later; only superseded is final.
.TP
.BI "show " ID
Print one ADR in full: context, decision, consequence, rationale.
.TP
.B list
List all decisions, accepted ones first.
.TP
.BI "supersede " "OLD NEW"
Mark OLD as superseded by NEW. NEW must already be accepted; a decision
cannot supersede itself, and only once.
.RE
.TP
.B stats
Print counters: open plans, todo / active / blocked / overdue tasks,
and tasks done today, in the last 7 days, and in total. Tasks finished
with resolution \fIabandoned\fR are excluded from the done counters.
.TP
.BI "generate " TARGET
Print a completion script for
.IR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " elvish " or " powershell
to stdout, or a roff manual page skeleton for
.IR man
(derived from the CLI definition; useful for cross\-checking flags).
Redirect into your shell's completion directory
(e.g.\& ~/.config/fish/completions/dp.fish).
.TP
.BI "help " "[COMMAND]"
Print help for dp or for one subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " FORMAT
Output format for read commands (\fBdp task list\fR, \fBdp task show\fR,
\fBdp stats\fR, \fBdp plan list/show\fR, \fBdp adr list\fR): \fBtable\fR
(default), \fBjson\fR or \fBmarkdown\fR. May be given before or after the
subcommand. In json mode stdout carries only JSON; empty results print
\fB[]\fR. Write commands ignore this flag and keep human\-readable
confirmations.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help; with a subcommand, print its help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH PRIORITIES
\fBlow\fR/0, \fBnormal\fR/1, \fBhigh\fR/2 and \fBurgent\fR/3; names and
numbers are interchangeable, names are case\-insensitive. A higher
number means more urgent. The default is \fBnormal\fR.
.SH STATES
Tasks have two axes. The
.I status
axis moves \fItodo\fR -> \fIactive\fR -> \fIdone\fR, with \fIblocked\fR as
a side state; \fBdp task start\fR records \fIstarted_at\fR (first start
only), \fBdp task done\fR and \fBdp task mod \-\-status done\fR record
\fIdone_at\fR, and moving to any other status clears it. The
.I resolution
axis classifies finished work: \fIdone\fR (completed), \fIabandoned\fR
(deliberately dropped) or \fIduplicated\fR; \fBdp task done\fR sets it
to \fIdone\fR by default. Verdicts carry their reasons:
\fIresolution_note\fR is permanent (recorded by \fB\-\-note\fR on
done/abandon/duplicate), \fIstatus_note\fR is process\-scoped (recorded
by \fBmod \-\-status \-\-note\fR, cleared on the next transition). A task
is overdue when its due date lies in the past and it is not done. The
boundary is completion: \fIabandoned\fR is excluded from output stats,
\fIduplicated\fR counts \(em the work was real, just misdirected; both
count toward plan progress.
.PP
Plans are containers with status \fIopen\fR or \fIarchived\fR
(\fBdp plan archive\fR); an archived plan keeps its progress as history.
.PP
Decisions move \fIproposed\fR -> \fIaccepted\fR -> \fIsuperseded\fR
(\fIrejected\fR is revisitable).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dp init
dp plan add "Q4 refactor auth" --due 2026-12-31 -p high
dp task add "Implement OAuth login" --plan 1 --due 2026-10-15 -p high -t auth,backend -d "OAuth2 auth code flow"
dp task list
dp task start 2
dp task mod 2 --status blocked --note "waiting on external API"
dp task list --overdue
dp task done 2
dp task duplicate 5 --of 3 --note "same flow, #3 has tests"
dp plan archive 1
dp adr add "Use SQLite" --context "Need zero-config embedded storage" --decision "rusqlite with bundled SQLite" --consequence "Single-file db, easy to back up"
dp adr accept 1
dp adr supersede 1 4
dp stats
dp task list --format=markdown
dp stats --format=json | jq .
dp generate fish > $HOME/.config/fish/completions/dp.fish
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .dp/dp.db
SQLite database for the project, created in the directory where
.B "dp init"
ran. Transient
.I .dp/dp.db\-wal
and
.I .dp/dp.db\-shm
files may sit next to it while dp is running.
.PP
The database is found by walking up from the current directory. With no
database in any parent directory, commands other than
.B init
fail and point at the current directory as the place to run
.BR init .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B dp
exits 0 on success (including \-\-help and \-\-version), 1 on runtime
failure with a diagnostic on stderr (database not initialized, unknown
id, invalid date or status, plan referenced by \fBdp task add \-\-plan\fR
does not exist), and 2 on usage errors detected by the argument parser.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1), git (1)
